-- title:
--   Kernel orders of G(T) on Pic⁰ as |Res(G,P)|
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field, $K$ an algebraically closed field, and let $F_0$ be a field which is a $k$-algebra and $F$ a field which is both a $K$-algebra and an $F_0$-algebra, with $F_0$ a curve over $k$ and $F$ a curve over $K$ in the project's sense: every nonzero element has a divisor recording its orders at all places and of degree zero, every place has residue field finite over the base, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one. Assume $F_0$ is generated over $k$ by a finite set, and that $K$ together with the image of $F_0$ generates $F$. Let $\varphi : F \to F$ be a $K$-algebra endomorphism which is integral as a ring homomorphism and which, on the image of $F_0$, is the $q$-th power map for $q = \#k$. Let $T$ be an additive endomorphism of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/K)$, the quotient of the group of degree-zero divisors by its subgroup of principal divisors, such that $T$ sends the class of a degree-zero divisor $D$ to the class of its push-forward along $\varphi$ (places restricted along $\varphi$, with multiplicities weighted by inertia degrees). Then there is a monic $P \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with $\deg P = 2g$, where $g = \dim_K H^1(0)$ is the genus of $F/K$, such that for every monic $G \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ whose constant coefficient has nonzero image in $K$: if $\mathrm{Res}(G,P) \neq 0$ then the kernel of the induced endomorphism $G(T)$ of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/K)$ has cardinality $|\mathrm{Res}(G,P)|$, and if $\mathrm{Res}(G,P) = 0$ then that kernel is infinite.
--
--   This is Weil's degree theory for the subring generated by the Frobenius endomorphism of a curve, in the form that $P$ plays the role of the characteristic polynomial of Frobenius and that the separable endomorphisms $G(\mathrm{Fr}_*)$ of the degree-zero divisor class group have kernel order equal to the absolute resultant $|\mathrm{Res}(G,P)|$. It is used to count fixed points of powers of Frobenius in [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.eq_of_natCard_ker_aeval_eq_natAbs_resultant_of_natCard_fixedPoints_restrictAlong_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.eq_of_natCard_ker_aeval_eq_natAbs_resultant_of_natCard_fixedPoints_restrictAlong_eq) and to control primary components of these kernels in [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_monic_natCard_primaryComponent_ker_aeval_of_pushforwardAlong_frobenius`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_monic_natCard_primaryComponent_ker_aeval_of_pushforwardAlong_frobenius).
